# Negative-control mutant — contract-product staged-import guard (AC-11)
#
# Scenario it must flip: contract-product.feature >
#   "A product still being imported cannot be changed"
# Test that goes red: contract-product.mutations.int.test.ts >
#   "AC-11 a staged product refuses stopRenewing and setConsolidation, sending no request to either endpoint"
#   (a staged row now lands on `available.status.active`, so STOP_RENEWING and
#   SET_CONSOLIDATION enter `processing` and a request is observed against
#   `.../modify_renew` and `.../properties`; both `toEqual([])` flip).
# Mutation: `selectStatusNode` drops the `stagedImport` arm, so a staged
#   import is placed by its raw `status.code` alone — the protection is gone.
# Collateral: contract-product.utils.test.ts >
#   "a staged import reads as STAGED regardless of its status.code" goes red
#   too — both tests guard this one line.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.utils.ts
index 34fab8669..937e5bc96 100644
